5497 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 5498 0 R/Alt(A black hole of mass M_BH on the left and a star of mass M_* and radius R_* at a distance r on the right. On the side of the star facing the black hole, the black hole pulls with acceleration G M_BH over (r minus R_*) squared, towards the black hole, while the self-gravity of the star pulls with G M_* over R_* squared, towards the center of the star. On the opposite side, both accelerations point towards the black hole: G M_BH over (r plus R_*) squared and G M_* over R_* squared.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[302]/Pg 17265 0 R>>
endobj
